<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capital_allocation" target="global_inflation_and_rat::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in AI-directed investment in specific jurisdictions attracts international venture and institutional capital chasing high-growth opportunities, increasing net inbound cross-border capital flows to those jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_inflation_and_rat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capital_allocation" target="global_inflation_and_rat::long_term_gov_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained large-scale AI investment raises corporate demand for long-term financing and boosts growth/term-premia expectations, which increases yields on long-maturity government debt as investors require higher compensation for duration and inflation risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_inflation_and_rat</data>
</edge>
