  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher shipping-transit risk elevates expected supply disruption and potential fiscal/insurance costs for affected states, widening sovereign term premia and pushing up long-term government yields in exposed markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">global_inflation_and_rat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::transit_risk_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising transit risk in Gulf shipping corridors forces rerouting, delays and temporary shortfalls in fuel and LNG deliveries that cascade into European markets supplying Ukraine, reducing short-term energy stability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::transit_risk_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_controls" id="0">
