<edge source="us_political_shift::power_balance_stock" target="global_inflation_and_rat::long_term_gov_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained shift in formal policymaking power toward a fiscal-expansionary majority raises market expectations of larger future deficits and higher term premia, directly repricing long-maturity government bonds upward.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">global_inflation_and_rat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_shift::power_balance_stock" target="iran_gulf_flashpoint::proxy_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A consolidation of formal policymaking power in a more hawkish executive enables quicker authorization of visible kinetic actions and naval interdictions in the Gulf, which Iran and its proxies respond to with increased indirect/deniable attacks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_shift::power_balance_stock" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A shift in formal power away from an executive willing/able to authorize large-scale military and financial support (e.g., stronger congressional restriction) reduces Ukraine's near-term combat sustainment and deterrence, encouraging Russia to raise the tempo and scale of kinetic operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_shift::power_balance_stock" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_controls" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A concentration of formal policymaking authority in national-security-oriented executive offices enables faster issuance of restrictive export-control rules and licensing changes that tighten limits on transfers of semiconductors, AI chips, and related know‑how to China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
