<edge source="us_political_shift::policy_uncertainty" target="global_inflation_and_rat::inflation_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp rise in near-term policy unpredictability leads firms to preemptively raise prices, build buffers, and for consumers and markets to demand inflation compensation, lifting short- to medium-term inflation expectations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">global_inflation_and_rat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_political_shift::policy_uncertainty" target="russia_ukraine_war::infra_resilience_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated uncertainty about near-term U.S. policy and funding commitments causes donors, contractors, and planners to delay reconstruction and hardening projects in Ukraine, reducing the region's infrastructure resilience as maintenance and upgrades are postponed.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_political_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
